$\begin{align}
\dfrac{a^{6}}{a^1}&=\dfrac{\overbrace{\cancel a\cdot a\cdot a\cdot a\cdot a\cdot a}^\text{6 times}}{\underbrace{\cancel a}_\text{1 time}}
\\\\\\
&=\underbrace{a\cdot a\cdot a\cdot a\cdot a}_\text{5 times}
\\\\
\end{align}$

When powers have the same base $\dfrac{x^m}{x^n}=x^{m-n}$. 

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{a^{6}}{a}&=\dfrac{a^{6}}{a^1}
\\\\
&=a^{6-1}
\\\\
&=a^5
\end{align}$
